WEBVTT

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:06.160
I've had countless Vanguard 
fights with Morikawa and Izaki,

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:10.520
And Misaki taught me the 
importance of grade 3s.

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:18.450
Give me the power! The proud, 
glorious white wings!

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:23.580
Ride! Solitary Knight, Gancelot!

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:27.510
But I lost to Kamui really easily.

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:31.430
Strange, but I feel like I've 
gotten better after losing.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:33.010
It's probably...

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:11.910
You've never been to a card shop 
other than Card Capital, have you?

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:13.050
N-No...

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:17.680
It's a whole lot of fun to have cardfights 
with a bunch of different people.

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:22.490
Now that you mention it, Kai said that 
he fights at a lot of different shops.

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:27.020
And you never know when you might have 
a fateful encounter with a rare card...

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:31.630
I can hear it! I can hear the voice of a 
rare card calling out to my card-fighting soul!

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.360
You're sure fired up, Morikawa.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.160
Well, sure! It's almost time 
for the shop tournament.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:37.410
Shop tournament?

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:38.750
You gonna enter, Aichi?

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:40.320
M-Me?

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:42.730
No way! I've still got a lot more to learn...

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:45.180
I'll work hard to cheer you on, Morikawa!

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:47.860
Sheesh, what a coward...

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:49.970
Sure! You can be my number one cheerleader!

00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:00.510
Strange... I was pretty sure there 
would be a card shop around here.

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:02.160
Hey, are we lost?

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.670
O-Of course not! <i>Me</i>? Be <i>lost</i>?

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:08.400
Rare card! Call to me once again!

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.160
I'm right here!

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:12.950
Just call out to me... while you still can!

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.750
Morikawa, Izaki...

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:19.050
Is that the store over there?

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:24.020
It seems kind of odd...

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:26.800
Each store has its own quirks, but...

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:28.610
Okay then! Aichi, you go first.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:35.520
The Mysterious Card Shop

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:40.990
Oh...? Customers...?

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:47.730
Excuse me! Is there anyone here?

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:50.400
What's with this place? The 
ceiling's a planetarium?

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:51.680
It's just a projection, right?

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:55.020
Quite different from Card 
Capital, that's for sure.

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:55.980
Yeah...

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:57.040
Hey!

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:58.300
Cards!

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:02.370
That's a Crested Dragon!

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:04.490
And that's a Stardrive Dragon!

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:07.890
These are all legendary cards 
that aren't sold anymore!

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:10.880
So it was <i>your</i> power that called me here!

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.300
Projections?

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:15.170
Welcome!

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:20.310
You've come to the card shop PSY!

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:21.490
PSY?

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:29.990
U-Um... Is there something...

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:32.420
Not really.

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:35.140
Please, come this way.

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:43.980
That's...

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:46.470
What is it?

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:48.980
A Vanguard fight stage!

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:51.720
A-Awesome!

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:55.250
It comes with play mats, too!

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:57.400
Is it okay if we use it?

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.170
Sure, go ahead.

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:02.290
If you <i>can</i>, that is.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:05.100
Morikawa, I'll try it too!

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:06.110
Sure thing!

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:07.780
Huh?

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:09.330
It's not working.

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:10.640
Where's the switch?

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:12.290
Is there a switch over there?

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:17.090
I don't see anything that 
looks like a switch.

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:18.920
It's perfectly smooth.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:25.950
<i>Please set your deck in place.</i>

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:28.730
<i>Please set your deck in place.</i>

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:29.760
R-Right!

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:40.750
The system activated?

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.510
Alright! Let's do this, Aichi!

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:44.490
Move!

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:47.290
Butting in, are we?

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:50.110
Try following basic etiquette, sheesh...

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.510
I mean, b-be my guest!

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:03.000
Um...

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:05.560
I am Kourin.

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:06.640
And you are...?

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:08.790
A-Aichi Sendou!

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:11.900
Show me how good you are.

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:14.450
You want a cardfight with me?

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:21.200
What's with that girl showing up?

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:22.660
Right, Morikawa?

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:25.050
Kourin... That's a good name.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:26.550
I've figured it out now.

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:29.810
It wasn't rare cards that called to me...

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:32.250
It was her!

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:34.750
Morikawa?

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:39.960
Aichi Sendou... I've never heard your name 
before. What tournaments have you won?

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:44.260
I-I've never participated in any tournaments!

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:52.590
He's never been in a tournament?

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:54.430
He's still a beginner.

00:06:56.110 --> 00:07:00.720
And even so, he gets invited to a 
cardfight with my darling Kourin!

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:02.560
I won't forgive him!

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:05.700
This has turned a little weird.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:09.690
But I get to have a cardfight 
using this amazing device.

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:10.530
Let's enjoy ourselves.

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:21.280
Anytime you're ready.

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:22.080
Right!

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:27.090
It's starting.

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:28.300
Stand up!

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:30.010
Vanguard!

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:32.840
Stardust Trumpeter!

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:35.330
Stardust Trumpeter!

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:46.940
Wow! The units are right before 
my eyes, and not just in my mind!

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:50.170
Why am I fighting someone at his level?

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:52.950
This is ridiculous. I'm 
going to end it quickly.

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:55.660
I'll go first.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:58.790
Draw! I ride the Flash Shield, Isolde!

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:04.530
M-My turn. Draw.

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:07.610
I also ride Isolde!

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:14.010
The same card...

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:16.890
Do you also use a Royal Paladin deck?

00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:19.890
Yes... Coincidentally.

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:24.110
I call Starlight Unicorn!

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:29.450
Isolde's power raises by 2000!

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:35.260
Solitary Knight, Gancelot.

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:39.280
I return this card to the deck, and 
choose one card to place in my hand.

00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:40.970
And that card is...

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:46.960
Oh? That's a rare card you've got there.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:50.840
Blaster Blade?

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:53.040
It's Aichi's trump card.

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:54.470
Even though it's a grade 2...

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:56.980
I attack Isolde with Unicorn!

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:01.260
Check for a damage trigger...

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:04.810
Trigger activated!

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:07.920
My Isolde's power raises by 5000!

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:14.640
Kourin's Isolde has a power of 11000.

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:17.740
My Isolde can't damage hers.

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:18.570
But...

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:22.820
If I get a trigger, I can damage her,

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:24.680
and if not, I add a card to my hand.

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:29.900
I attack Kourin's Isolde with my Isolde!

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:33.880
Check for a drive trigger!

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:35.760
No trigger.

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:40.270
My turn is over.

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:42.500
My turn. Draw.

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:44.290
I ride Tristan.

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:53.000
And I call Starlight Unicorn and Flogal.

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:01.490
I attack with Unicorn!

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:05.500
Damage check...

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:08.410
Trigger activated!

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:11.130
Isolde's power is raised by 5000!

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:15.210
I attack once again with Tristan!

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:15.960
Flogal!

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:20.740
Check for a drive trigger.

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:28.690
She made a comeback!

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:31.690
Alright! You rock, Kourin my sweet!

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:35.960
You took damage, but I did not.

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:39.450
I wonder if you know what 
made the difference?

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:41.410
My little beginner...

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:00.380
Your friend is pitiful.

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:02.200
But he's still a beginner.

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:05.380
And this Kourin girl seems pretty strong.

00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:06.640
Maybe he should throw in the towel?

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:08.770
No. Showing weakness is never good.

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:10.080
Morikawa...

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:13.270
I see... So this was all to 
teach him about harsh reality!

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:16.730
It's punishment for fighting 
my sweet Kourin before me!

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:19.580
Aichi! I hope you're reduced 
to a shriveled, sniveling mess!

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:23.320
I think your other friend is pitiful, too.

00:11:26.210 --> 00:11:27.670
Poor thing.

00:11:29.110 --> 00:11:30.910
Don't bully him <i>too</i> much, now.

00:11:35.870 --> 00:11:37.880
How long are you going to make me wait?

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:39.580
If you're going to give 
up, then do it already.

00:11:39.580 --> 00:11:41.900
W-Wait! I'm not giving up!

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:44.480
I apologize for making you wait.

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:48.170
I was thinking about how I could 
make up for my earlier mistake.

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:51.440
Oh? Still trying hard, are we?

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:54.350
My turn! Stand and draw!

00:11:57.870 --> 00:11:59.700
I don't want to give up.

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:02.460
Because I want to show her 
how I fight with this card.

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:06.400
Stand up, my avatar!

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:09.120
Ride! Blaster Blade!

00:12:21.110 --> 00:12:23.520
Ooh, now that's cool!

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:26.050
That's Blaster Blade?

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:29.270
Wingal!

00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:33.020
Plus, I move Unicorn back, and call Gallatin!

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:45.820
Give me the power...

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:50.030
Blaster Blade.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:56.720
Everyone, let's go!

00:13:04.230 --> 00:13:06.400
Gallatin, attack Tristan!

00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:10.360
With Unicorn's boost, 
Gallatin's power is 16000!

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:15.390
I guard with Epona from my hand!

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:25.240
Wingal!

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:33.670
Alright! With Wingal's 
support, he's powered up!

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:37.170
Plus, Wingal's skill adds another +4000!

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:43.590
Attack!

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:50.880
Check for a drive trigger...

00:13:51.420 --> 00:13:52.900
No trigger.

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:54.600
No trigger for me, either.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:57.340
Damn! She took damage!

00:13:57.340 --> 00:13:58.600
My Kourin!

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:00.580
You know what you're doing, I see...

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:02.000
Little beginner.

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:04.540
My turn.

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:06.120
Stand and draw!

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:11.480
Ride the Crimson Butterfly, Brigitte!

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:16.160
And I call one more as well.

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:21.380
I move Unicorn back,

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:22.880
and call Tristan!

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:28.390
Alright! She's got two grade 3s!

00:14:28.390 --> 00:14:30.310
Aichi, you're through!

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:33.810
Two grade 3s?

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:36.520
Brigitte, attack Blaster Blade!

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:41.150
Epona, protect Blaster Blade!

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:49.810
Will you be able to guard 
against the next one, I wonder?

00:14:55.630 --> 00:14:56.760
Attack!

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:01.880
Blaster Blade!

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:04.040
Check first card for Twin Drive.

00:15:04.410 --> 00:15:05.550
No trigger.

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:08.390
But Gancelot is a grade 3.

00:15:08.390 --> 00:15:12.800
So by Brigitte's skill, his power raises 
by 5000 through the end of this turn!

00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:18.120
Second check.

00:15:23.170 --> 00:15:24.870
Trigger activated!

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:26.820
Brigitte's critical +1!

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:31.030
And I add +5000 to Tristan, 
who has yet to attack!

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:36.770
Burn to ash, Blaster Blade!

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:43.290
You go, Kourin my honey!

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:46.320
Burn me with your flames, too!

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:00.110
Attack!

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:06.800
That makes 5.

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:11.860
Trigger activated!

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:14.860
I recover one card from my damage zone.

00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:22.300
So, you drew a heal trigger now?

00:16:22.300 --> 00:16:23.790
My turn is over.

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:25.650
He managed to make it through, somehow.

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:27.500
Does this guy ever know 
when to call it quits?

00:16:27.810 --> 00:16:29.300
My turn.

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:30.820
Stand and draw!

00:16:33.820 --> 00:16:38.470
If I leave Isolde in my hand, I can 
probably prevent taking damage next turn.

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:43.060
But, if I attack with full 
force, and get a trigger...

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:48.710
I can't be sure I'll be able 
to defend against everything.

00:16:48.710 --> 00:16:49.610
So in that case...

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:52.650
Give me power!

00:16:52.850 --> 00:16:54.990
The proud, glorious white wings!

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:55.980
Ride!

00:16:57.160 --> 00:16:59.620
Solitary Knight, Gancelot!

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:04.730
Aichi's finally got one 
of your favorite grade 3s!

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:05.870
Keep quiet about that, sheesh...

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:07.440
Counterblast!

00:17:07.890 --> 00:17:09.500
Power +5000!

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:13.200
And once more!

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:19.770
He's activating his Counterblast twice?

00:17:19.770 --> 00:17:21.810
Plus, I call Marron and Isolde!

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:26.810
Aichi's usually so timid, but he's 
sure going all out this time!

00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:35.490
Gallatin, attack!

00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:41.950
Epona!

00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:48.670
Marron, attack!

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:57.260
Wingal!

00:18:09.050 --> 00:18:12.370
Go!!

00:18:12.370 --> 00:18:13.780
Twin drive check!

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:15.200
First check...

00:18:16.870 --> 00:18:17.780
No.

00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:20.100
Come on...

00:18:21.110 --> 00:18:22.550
Be a trigger...

00:18:31.310 --> 00:18:33.480
Looks like you didn't get it.

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:35.760
Right. No trigger...

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:40.190
Check for a damage trigger...

00:18:41.330 --> 00:18:42.390
Second...

00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:45.850
Third...

00:18:49.950 --> 00:18:51.780
Heal trigger, activated!

00:18:52.370 --> 00:18:54.360
I recover 1 damage.

00:18:57.280 --> 00:18:59.990
My turn. Stand and draw.

00:19:00.540 --> 00:19:01.990
I call Isolde!

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:09.320
If you're expecting to get 
another heal trigger...

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:11.790
It's not over yet.

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:14.080
There's got to be a way!

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:17.220
I attack Gancelot with Brigitte!

00:19:19.230 --> 00:19:20.550
Guard with Flogal!

00:19:24.820 --> 00:19:25.630
Next!

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:29.980
I... do not guard.

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:32.230
Aichi! Just give up already!

00:19:32.660 --> 00:19:35.440
Why isn't he defending?

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:37.910
Only one more...

00:19:37.910 --> 00:19:40.240
As long as she doesn't get that card...

00:19:48.680 --> 00:19:53.590
I admit that your timing while going 
all-out last turn had merit, beginner.

00:19:53.590 --> 00:19:54.710
But...

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:56.210
This is as far as you get.

00:19:58.810 --> 00:20:00.020
No!

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:04.680
Critical trigger, activated!

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:23.050
So, how do you activate this thing?

00:20:23.050 --> 00:20:25.580
Sorry! The batteries ran out!

00:20:25.580 --> 00:20:27.930
It runs on batteries?

00:20:27.930 --> 00:20:30.580
I really do have a lot to learn.

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:33.040
That hand...

00:20:33.810 --> 00:20:36.520
He didn't give in, to the very end.

00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:37.510
Thank you!

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:40.970
I may have lost, but it was a lot of fun.

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:45.510
Nice fight, you two.

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:47.170
Suiko!

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:51.660
Here.

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:53.970
The King of Knights, Alfred!

00:20:54.550 --> 00:20:56.020
You're giving this card to me?

00:20:56.340 --> 00:20:58.270
Consider it a memento of your visit here.

00:20:58.560 --> 00:21:01.090
T-Thank you very much!

00:21:01.460 --> 00:21:02.430
Tournament...

00:21:03.350 --> 00:21:05.360
Enter a tournament.

00:21:05.970 --> 00:21:09.490
When you get stronger, I'll fight you again.

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:10.990
Really?

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:13.510
Kourin, my darling!

00:21:13.510 --> 00:21:16.290
Have a Vanguard fight with me next!

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:18.840
Oopsie! It's closing time!

00:21:19.610 --> 00:21:22.000
Alfred? Cool.

00:21:27.490 --> 00:21:30.380
The boy will surely come again.

00:21:38.660 --> 00:21:40.020
It's gone!

00:21:40.370 --> 00:21:42.280
What's gone, Morikawa?

00:21:42.530 --> 00:21:45.030
That shop! My beautiful Kourin's shop!

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:46.640
I've searched all over for it, but it's gone!

00:21:46.640 --> 00:21:47.960
Maybe they went out of business.

00:21:47.960 --> 00:21:49.320
They didn't have any customers, remember?

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:53.700
No! I haven't even fought 
with my baby Kourin!

00:21:53.700 --> 00:21:54.540
Shut up.

00:21:54.740 --> 00:21:56.900
Aichi... What shop?

00:21:56.900 --> 00:21:58.340
It was in the city.

00:21:58.340 --> 00:22:01.300
The units were right in front of 
your eyes... actually fighting!

00:22:01.300 --> 00:22:02.720
It was really cool.

00:22:02.720 --> 00:22:03.250
Wasn't it?

00:22:03.250 --> 00:22:06.660
I'm gonna die if I can't see her!

00:22:06.660 --> 00:22:08.430
I'm gonna die of a broken heart!

00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:09.510
At least you'd be quiet then!

00:22:09.810 --> 00:22:12.510
Was there a shop like that?

00:23:51.260 --> 00:23:54.360
Aichi, was that PSY shop big?

00:23:54.360 --> 00:23:55.110
Was it clean and neat?

00:23:55.110 --> 00:23:56.270
Did it have lots of customers?

00:23:56.270 --> 00:23:58.130
Shin, you're being too competitive.

00:23:58.130 --> 00:24:01.410
But doesn't it make you wonder? Right, Aichi?

00:24:02.430 --> 00:24:05.640
But the most amazing part was how the 
units came to life before your eyes.

00:24:05.640 --> 00:24:08.420
Yeah, that might be tricky 
to set up in Card Capital.

00:24:08.650 --> 00:24:10.630
But having a standing fight...

00:24:10.630 --> 00:24:12.320
He's plotting something...

00:24:12.320 --> 00:24:14.910
Next time: The Fearsome Soulblast!

00:24:14.910 --> 00:24:18.300
The fight between Kai and Kamui 
will trigger pictures in my mind!
